\periph Old Testament Introduction
\mt1 Introduction to the Hebrew Scriptures (Old Testament)
\p The Hebrew scriptures are a record of Yisrael's experience of what God is like and what the people who worship God should be like. It declares the god Yahweh as the creator of the world and it tells how God blesses people and establishes relations with people through agreements that he makes with them.
…

\periph Pentateuch Introduction
\s1 The Torah (Pentateuch)
\p ‘Torah’ (from Hebrew) means ‘instructions’, and ‘Pentateuch’ (from Greek) is a term that means ‘five scrolls (books)’ and is used to describe the five accounts that are positioned at the beginning of both Jewish and Christian Bibles.
…

\periph History Introduction
\s1 Historical Books
\p The documents in this section describe important events in Yisrael's history. It begins with descriptions of how the people entered Kena’an/Canaan, the land which God promised to Abraham and Sarah and their descendants, and goes on to describe the time of Yisrael's great kings (Sha’ul/Saul, David, and Shelomoh/Solomon) and the division of Yisrael into two kingdoms (Yisrael/Israel in the north and Yehudah/Judah in the south) who often found themselves in conflict.
